ing its source and edition, and a missing or stale corpus is an error that names the fix, never an empty result. rfclib covers the RFC series, itulib the ITU-T ASN.1 and X.500 text the RFCs cannot reach, and zimlore language and framework documentation from Kiwix ZIM files, with the edition date and age of what it read.","id":"reference","title":"Reference libraries: the context a task needs"},{"blurb":"Generated shells and plans, by tier and wave. Each has an obligation matrix tied to the RFCs it implements.","id":"planned","title":"Planned SDKs"},{"blurb":"Launchers, infrastructure modules, and MCP servers that give agents a narrow, audited interface to a program.","id":"tools","title":"Tools and MCP servers"},{"blurb":"Reverse engineering and test doubles for printers, scanners and network gear.","id":"re","title":"Hardware and firmware"},{"blurb":"Libraries and applications outside the planned portfolio.","id":"other","title":"Other projects"},{"blurb":"Upstream projects carried with changes of our own.","id":"forks","title":"Forks with work on top"},{"blurb":"Older projects, kept for the record.","id":"archive","title":"Earlier work"}],"source":{"commit":"3cfc71542a868c0da2efd19d0610cf392c8d4986","repo":"b1tninja/sdk-forge (workspace)"}}
